The module src/aphrody/jan_adk.py is a semantic adapter informed by the Jan
Python and JavaScript/TypeScript ADKs, source revision
14a720628f9592c8e60f7e081ef733076db8a6a9, at:
  https://github.com/janhq/jan/tree/14a720628f9592c8e60f7e081ef733076db8a6a9/adk/python
  https://github.com/janhq/jan/tree/14a720628f9592c8e60f7e081ef733076db8a6a9/packages/adk
Those ADK package manifests declare AGPL-3.0 and identify Jan
<service@jan.ai> as author. The Aphrody adapter retains AGPL-3.0-only source
notices. Jan's repository-root Apache-2.0 license is not a substitute for the
ADK package licenses. No Jan runtime binary or model weights are included.

The canonical app-server transport, src/aphrody/agent.py, includes portions
derived from openai/codex sdk/python/src/openai_codex/{client,_message_router}.py
at revision 78245b47af2a7aafcabe025828ceecca69db4df1 (Apache-2.0), as recorded
in that module. These transport notices are retained.

The native math extension is the Rust crate crates/ai/rag-python (package
aphrody-rust, Apache-2.0) of the Aphrody monorepo, built in place with the
workspace Cargo.lock together with crates/ai/rag-core. This is provenance, not
proof of a newly compiled wheel or compatibility with every Yolo runtime/platform.
